      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We’re partnering with Blue Origin on the first heavy-lift launch for Project Suncatcher, our long-term moonshot to scale AI infrastructure in space by tapping into the abundant solar power in orbit.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/blue-origin-project-suncatcher-partnership/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T19:00:43.607Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Targeted for Q1 2029, Blue Origin’s heavy-lift New Glenn rocket will deploy our satellites — each with roughly the capacity of a data center rack — into sun-synchronous orbit.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/blue-origin-project-suncatcher-partnership/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-19T19:00:43.607Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This dedicated launch builds on our ongoing work with other satellite and launch partners and represents a crucial milestone on our long-term roadmap as we expand the boundaries of what's possible for the future of compute.",
